    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0366" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7056: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Legation in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-16T15:00:00+08:00">June 16, 1935—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>165. Shanghai’s 315, June 15, 9 a.m.<anchor n="83" xml:id="d211-f1"/> Director of
                    Department of Information and Publicity of the Foreign Office has informed me
                    that <pb facs="0367" n="255" xml:id="pg255"/> censorship has been lifted on
                    press despatches concerning situation in North China and an American newspaper
                    correspondent from Shanghai confirms this statement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
